      "title": "Route 53 Mental Model: Zones and Records",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Route 53 Mental Model: Zones and Records",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Zones and Records",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Hosted zone== = container of records for one domain",
                "{green:Public}: answers internet queries",
                "{purple:Private}: answers only from associated VPCs",
                "New zone gives **4 NS records**; they must match the registrar's name servers"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Record = name + type + value + TTL",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`A`",
                  "IPv4 address"
                ],
                [
                  "`AAAA`",
                  "IPv6 address"
                ],
                [
                  "`CNAME`",
                  "name to another name"
                ],
                [
                  "`MX`",
                  "mail"
                ],
                [
                  "`TXT`",
                  "verification text"
                ],
                [
                  "`NS`",
                  "delegates a subdomain"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. CNAME vs Alias",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "CNAME",
                "Alias"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Zone apex (example.com)",
                  "{red:not allowed}",
                  "{green:works}"
                ],
                [
                  "Query cost",
                  "billed",
                  "free for AWS targets"
                ],
                [
                  "Returns",
                  "another name",
                  "A/AAAA directly"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Targets: ==CloudFront==, ALB/NLB, API Gateway, S3 website endpoint",
                "Also Elastic Beanstalk, or another record in the same zone",
                "An alias **cannot** point to an EC2 DNS name"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistake",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "example.com",
                    "sub": "A alias, no TTL to set",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "d111abcdef8.cloudfront.net",
                    "sub": "inherits target's TTL",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Zone recreated?",
              "text": "Update the registrar NS to the new hosted zone's NS. Stale NS means DNS ==resolves nowhere=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Routing Policies and Health Checks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Routing Policies and Health Checks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Simple, Weighted, Latency",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Policy",
                "Answers with",
                "Key fact"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Simple",
                  "one or more values, random order",
                  "==no health checks== on it"
                ],
                [
                  "Weighted",
                  "share = weight / sum of weights",
                  "weight `0` stops traffic"
                ],
                [
                  "Latency",
                  "region with lowest latency",
                  "record tagged with a region"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Weighted records share a name; weights ==0-255==",
                "Weighted fits {blue:canary} and {green:blue-green}",
                "Latency is measured from the **user to AWS regions**, not to your server"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Failover",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q"
                  ],
                  [
                    "a",
                    "b"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q": {
                    "text": "Primary healthy?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "a": {
                    "text": "Serve primary",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  "b": {
                    "text": "Serve secondary",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "a",
                    "label": "yes"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "b",
                    "label": "no"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Active-passive==: one primary, one secondary record",
                "The primary **needs a health check**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Geolocation and Geoproximity",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Geolocation==: by user's country or continent (compliance, localisation)",
                "==Geoproximity==: needs **Traffic Flow**, shifted with ==bias=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Add a Default record",
              "text": "Geolocation needs a ==Default== record. Without it, users from unmatched locations get no answer."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Health Checks and Everyday Route 53 Usage",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Health Checks and Everyday Route 53 Usage",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Health check types",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Watches",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Endpoint==",
                  "HTTP, HTTPS or TCP target",
                  "public endpoints"
                ],
                [
                  "==Calculated==",
                  "other health checks",
                  "combine with AND/OR"
                ],
                [
                  "==CloudWatch alarm==",
                  "an alarm state",
                  "private resources"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Interval {blue:30s} by default, {blue:10s} fast",
                "Unhealthy after {red:3} failed checks by default",
                "Checkers sit **outside your VPC**: private endpoint needs an ==alarm check==",
                "Public endpoint: allow the Route 53 ==health checker IP ranges== in the security group"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Everyday commands",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Create or update a record: ==UPSERT== inside `change.json`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \\",
                "  --hosted-zone-id Z123 \\",
                "  --change-batch file://change.json"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check an answer with `dig`, or ask Route 53 itself"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "dig example.com +short",
                "aws route53 test-dns-answer --hosted-zone-id Z123 \\",
                "  --record-name example.com --record-type A"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No health check attached",
              "text": "A failover or weighted record with **no health check** keeps sending traffic to a dead endpoint. An ==alias== record can use **Evaluate Target Health** instead of a separate check."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CloudFront Distributions, Origins and Cache Behaviours",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CloudFront Distributions, Origins and Cache Behaviours",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Distribution and Origins",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Viewer",
                    "sub": "request",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Edge location",
                    "sub": "hit: serve",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Regional edge cache",
                    "sub": "edge miss",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Origin",
                    "sub": "cache miss",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Distribution== = CDN config with a `*.cloudfront.net` domain",
                "Origins: **S3 bucket**, **ALB**, **API Gateway**, any custom HTTP server",
                "==Origin group== = failover to a secondary origin on 5xx or 4xx"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Behaviours and Cache Key",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Behaviour matches a ==path pattern==: `/images/*`, `/api/*`",
                "Picks origin, allowed methods, cache policy, viewer protocol policy (redirect HTTP to HTTPS)",
                "Patterns are checked ==in order==; `Default (*)` is last"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Cache key== = path + forwarded headers, cookies, query strings",
                "More forwarded values = {red:lower hit ratio}",
                "Forward only what the origin needs"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Policy",
                "Forwarded to origin",
                "In cache key"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Cache policy",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Origin request policy",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Custom Domain Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Certificate and CNAME",
              "text": "The ACM certificate must be in ==us-east-1==. The domain also needs an **alternate domain name (CNAME)** set on the distribution."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "TTLs, Invalidations and OAC for S3",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TTLs, Invalidations and OAC for S3",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. TTL and Invalidation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Origin ==max-age== or ==s-maxage== is honoured, clamped to policy **Minimum TTL** and **Maximum TTL**",
                "No cache header from origin: ==Default TTL== {blue:86400s}",
                "Invalidation removes the object from {red:every edge}; takes minutes",
                "First ==1,000 paths/month== free"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws cloudfront create-invalidation \\",
                "  --distribution-id E123 \\",
                "  --paths \"/index.html\" \"/img/*\""
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "tip",
              "title": "Better than invalidating",
              "text": "Versioned names (`app.v3.js` or a content hash) are a **new URL**: no invalidation, long TTLs are safe."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. OAC for a Private S3 Bucket",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==OAC== signs requests to S3 with **SigV4**; bucket stays public-blocked",
                "Replaces legacy ==OAI==; supports SSE-KMS and all regions"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Bucket policy",
                "Value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Principal",
                  "`cloudfront.amazonaws.com`"
                ],
                [
                  "Action",
                  "`s3:GetObject`"
                ],
                [
                  "Condition",
                  "`StringEquals` `AWS:SourceArn` = distribution ARN"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "S3 **website endpoint** has no OAC support. Use the ==REST endpoint== origin."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Hot file changed?** Version the name, or invalidate the path",
                "**Why OAC?** Private bucket, CloudFront only, via SourceArn"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
